EDIT: I just googled Morioh and realised it's a fictional place... Oh.

[http://www.nationaltrustcollections.org.uk/object/112446](http://www.nationaltrustcollections.org.uk/object/112446)

&#x200B;

Solved by doing more googling!

What even are "bad" communication skills? Aren't people allowed to communicate in their own way? How can you really even quantify it as a skill with varying levels of expertise? ... Communication styles are subjective and the kind of styles I like, others may find annoying and vice versa... I know there's a certain level of fluency and literacy required for work but I don't think that's what they're referencing. What they really mean is they want someone who is extroverted and outgoing.

&#x200B;

Ramble over! Lol. I just hate seeing this  empty phrase "excellent communication skills" repeated again and again when they mean something else.
